{"title":"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Motivation_for_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Motivation for Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/7975e5a534f64849617469be501a5e56286faf72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> has six consecutive zeros in its decimal representation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of a number be the units digit, digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the tens digit, and so on. Let the 6 consecutive zeroes be at digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2a1538a16b3397245b56dbfb7e4f2670948007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> through digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. The criterion is then obviously equivalent to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b87b06269523ee8bce36e8084669bb52fc8a936.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^n \\bmod 10^k &lt; 10^{k-6}\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f6b0a7f6e5491d99add69272996a1e8875d09c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20+2^{19}, k = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies this, thus proving the problem statement (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/51678762981dabddfda854947e90e43dc76b9a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20+2^{19} &lt; 10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" />). \n</p><p>We want \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f52835ea07e1e2561865e59f564ffecfb4d26d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{20+2^{19}}\\pmod{10^{20}}\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>We can split this into its prime factors. Obviously, it is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cc39c93c350a7c65e1b10bbd0b5e8385080b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />, so we only need to consider it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6ae4b95cc87b72b1e3f4d8b60eed955bf402fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod2^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67affe804e98dfb0974ff8e993ee1bf7d4c88c8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{20}\\cdot5^{2^{19}}\\pmod{2^{20}}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf763a002851293d25dd049c64b1253f57f8451b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{20}\\cdot5^{\\varphi(2^{20})}\\pmod{2^{20}}\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921aade3100afbc11d0d13f71cdd7e68d83ad52e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> is the Euler Totient Function.) By Euler's Theorem, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e6f8df11e899923aabd42009cf1c57defdb05a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigl(5, 2^{20}\\bigr)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"92\" height=\"24\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6bc439266550cb49c86bd3e0283e04fe76c0f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{\\varphi(2^{20})}\\equiv1\\pmod{2^{20}}\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0bc1035a9bf5e1975c1ca6ca363d9dad5872b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{20}\\cdot5^{\\varphi (2^{20})}\\equiv5^{20}\\pmod{2^{20}}\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19ad23010d7f34b6aba43a7b977492b20b895eeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{20} &gt; 10^6, 5^{20} &lt; 10^{14} = 10^{20-6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b87b06269523ee8bce36e8084669bb52fc8a936.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^n \\bmod 10^k &lt; 10^{k-6}\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4e0a88cc2b69bbfe125092bae8dc66b690f09f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20+2^{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfb829b53157a5147881107e8e92843817a5a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, and thus the problem statement has been proven. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Motivation_for_Solution\">Motivation for Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Motivation for Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Modifying our necessary and sufficient inequality, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51fd401a20dd2fdc46bdb060ef8e5d2f8d6f161f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^n \\mod 10^k &lt; 10^{k-6}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcc2a2170799f68cf10c8fffd70c540c29926ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^k \\left(5^{n-k} \\mod 2^k\\right) &lt; 10^{k-6}\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/7865ca3755556b9de468d2fd9153b16e3a744a4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{n-k} \\mod 2^k &lt; \\frac{2^{k-6}}{5^6}\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Since gcd<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f422fee640fcab8c8a7e82038999d875a94a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(5^{n-k}, 2^k\\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"109\" height=\"22\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e382be12e5c9272e25f196b60dab1752cd07077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> (which is obviously true) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488595b52b4cf4e5dd40c0ee64e556fd5e68d318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> which is also true given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f613daeb59f8ac072695ac1a1a7e45de2e4cab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^k &lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" />, we need the RHS to be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/21288ecdd861b9bc60ea16310261618a8d93c6bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2^{k-6}}{5^6} &gt; 1\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0dea000d69f61209866be85923c8d4c2ef79d20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{k-6} &gt; 5^6\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/937416acd0e5df5818974dd1cddd563d6a3baa68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^k &gt; 10^6\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfies this inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfb829b53157a5147881107e8e92843817a5a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, so we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfb829b53157a5147881107e8e92843817a5a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1bd3d90b9c94e2f4f89b147f7dc83a5a7da918.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{n-20} \\mod 2^{20} &lt; \\frac{2^{14}}{5^6}\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f61d85df3f0e18a3db963b02e97b78dbfc38c4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{n-20} \\mod 2^{20} \\leq 1\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/facbe61a5028bb9ee5c2e439ad5b59a55150aff1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{n-20} \\mod 2^{20} = 1\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>From this, Euler's Theorem comes to mind and we see that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/156db9ad34239117dea9ff39a3adbf76171d34cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-20 = \\varphi\\left(2^{20}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"127\" height=\"22\" />, the equality is satisfied. Thus, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f3276762886dd24515eecf7fceab4389f4402463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20 + 2^{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />, which is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d09267a29bc4ec950a006fe23bfb45f7700b680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, and we should be done. However, this requires slightly more formalization, and can be proven directly more easily if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4e0a88cc2b69bbfe125092bae8dc66b690f09f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20+2^{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> is known or suspected. \n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO\" title=\"2016 USAJMO\">2016 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2016 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 268/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7938/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   24.296      1 -total\n 77.41%   18.807      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 21.89%    5.318      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14948:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002401 and revision id 190622. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}